# @j0nathan-ll0yd/* (portal-contract, config) resolve from GitHub Packages.
# Registry mapping ONLY — the auth token is intentionally NOT committed here.
# pnpm IGNORES an env-expanded `//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}`
# in a project-level .npmrc (it warns "Ignored project-level auth setting" on
# every command); npm expands it but pnpm does not. Local auth comes from the
# machine-global ~/.npmrc; CI sets it at the user level via
# `pnpm config set '//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken'` (see the workflows'
# "Authenticate to GitHub Packages" step). See atlas decision 0015.
@j0nathan-ll0yd:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
